    "n5.faq.a1": "Yes, appraisal documentation is delivered in certified bilingual format (Spanish/English) for risk committees, reinsurance, and international brokers.",
    "n5.faq.q2": "What is the difference between replacement value and market value?",
    "n5.faq.a2": "Replacement value corresponds to the cost of replacing the piece in its legitimate market; market value reflects the real auction or sale quotation. Which applies depends on the purpose of the policy.",
    "n5.faq.q3": "Are audits handled for collections located outside Cuba?",
    "n5.faq.a3": "The methodology applied carries international validity; audit logistics are evaluated based on the collection's location and scope.",

    "n6.faq.title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "n6.faq.q1": "What type of institutions can request this appraisal?",
    "n6.faq.a1": "Museums, scientific entities, heritage institutions, and underwater archaeological research organizations.",
    "n6.faq.q2": "Does the appraisal include conservation recommendations?",
    "n6.faq.a2": "The authenticity and historical significance opinion includes the descriptive study needed for designing consolidation treatments, without carrying out the conservation work itself.",
    "n6.faq.q3": "Is the physical artifact required for the initial appraisal?",
