    "n1.hero.h1": "Fine Art Appraisal & Authentication for Private Collectors",
    "n1.hero.subtitle": "Independent technical opinions on authenticity, cataloguing, and economic valuation for art owners, collectors, and investors of high-value assets.",
    "n1.value.text": "Luis Manuel Almeida Luis practices appraisal under a strict zero-conflict-of-interest principle: he neither buys nor sells works of art, nor charges fees as a percentage of the appraised value. Each opinion is an independent technical judgment, the result of more than 40 years documenting, cataloguing, and appraising Cuban and Ibero-American cultural heritage, with over 20,000 works of art and heritage assets inventoried throughout his career.",
    "n1.problem.text": "Acquiring or custodianship of art without an independent expert opinion exposes the owner to forgery, speculative overvaluation, and legal indefensibility in commercial or succession transactions.",
    "n1.cases.title": "Documented Cases",
    "n1.case.1": "Inventory and cataloguing of the collections of René Portocarrero (1988) and Fayad Jamís (1988).",
    "n1.case.2": "Inventory of the collections of Sandú Darié (1993) and Luis Alberto Quintero (1999).",
    "n1.case.3": "Inventory of the estates of Gilma Madera, Marta Jiménez, and Armando Suárez del Villar.",
    "n1.case.4": "Appraisal of exceptional assets of Cuban Cultural Heritage classified as Grade I Value (2005).",
