    "n1.service.3": "Economic Valuation Appraisal Report.",
    "n1.service.4": "Condition Report.",
    "n1.cta.whatsapp": "Hello, I am a private collector/owner of works of art and would like to request a confidential consultation on appraisal and authentication.",
    "n1.cta.form": "Submit a Confidential Engagement Brief",

    // === NICHO 2: Teaching (docencia-conferencias.html) ===
    "n2.hero.h1": "Teaching, Lectures & Training in Fine Art & Heritage Appraisal",
    "n2.hero.subtitle": "Academic modules, keynote lectures, and specialized training for universities, museums, customs authorities, law enforcement, and cultural heritage institutions.",
    "n2.value.text": "With more than 25 years of active university teaching, Luis Manuel Almeida Luis serves as Associate Professor at the University of the Arts (ISA, 2001–present), the University of Havana (2001–present), and the San Gerónimo University College of Havana (2012–present). His academic work is reinforced by specialized publications and direct collaboration with international heritage organizations.",
    "n2.problem.text": "Lack of rigorous technical training in appraisal and expert appraisal fosters critical errors in heritage protection, the detection of forgeries, and customs control against international illicit trafficking.",
    "n2.cases.title": "Documented Cases (institutions and organizations)",
    "n2.case.1": "International courses and diplomas: Fundación de Museos Nacionales (Venezuela, 2007), IARTES and IPC (Venezuela, 2010), University of Panama (2015), IBERMUSEOS (Costa Rica, 2018).",
    "n2.case.2": "Joint lecture on Illicit Trafficking with Italy's Carabinieri TPC unit (Havana, 2018).",
    "n2.case.3": "Academic publications in UNESCO's Cultura y Desarrollo journal: \"Control en las aduanas cubanas\" and \"El Valor de las Obras de Arte\" (2013).",
    "n2.case.4": "Co-author of two chapters in Dr. Alex J. Rosenberg's book Tasación de Obras de Arte, Ludwig Foundation / National Council of Cultural Heritage (2010).",
    "n2.services.title": "Specific Appraisal Services",
    "n2.service.1": "University academic modules on fine art valuation and appraisal.",
    "n2.service.2": "Specialized keynote lectures.",
    "n2.service.3": "Workshops on the prevention of illicit trafficking of cultural property.",
    "n2.service.4": "Appraisal protocols and antique-recognition training.",
    "n2.cta.main": "Request an Academic Proposal",
    "n2.cta.whatsapp": "Hello, I represent a university/cultural institution and would like to inquire about availability for an academic module or lecture on art and heritage appraisal.",
    "n2.cta.form": "Submit an Academic Collaboration Request",

    // === NICHO 3: Estates (herencias-sucesiones.html) ===
    "n3.hero.h1": "Estate & Inheritance Art Appraisal Services",
    "n3.hero.subtitle": "Independent technical inventory and valuation of works of art and heritage assets for inheritance declarations, probate, and notarial or tax-related partition.",
    "n3.value.text": "As a Partition Appraiser (Perito Tasador-Partidor), Luis Manuel Almeida Luis combines technical asset analysis with the mediation required for an equitable distribution among heirs. He has carried out more than 15 estate liquidation processes throughout his career, maintaining strict professional confidentiality over private family estates and testamentary matters that are not disclosed publicly.",
    "n3.problem.text": "Hereditary partition of artistic assets generates severe family disputes and fiscal imbalances before Notary or Tax Authority if not mediated by an equitable and mathematically unassailable technical valuation. When each heir distrusts the others' judgment of value, disagreement over a single painting or collection can become the fracture point for an entire family.",
