    // === NICHO 4: Lawyers (abogados-notarios.html) ===
    "n4.hero.h1": "Forensic Art Appraiser for Litigation, Probate & Notarial Proceedings",
    "n4.hero.subtitle": "Judicial-grade appraisal reports and expert technical assistance for civil litigation, probate proceedings, marital dissolutions, and estate division.",
    "n4.value.text": "Luis Manuel Almeida Luis serves as a technical expert in probate proceedings and litigation before judicial and notarial authorities, backed by 41 years as the specialist responsible for airport customs and cultural property seizures (1988–2024), including cases whose findings were formally ratified before judicial authority. His expert function is exercised with the same technical independence required in Cuba's representation before international legal forums.",
    "n4.problem.text": "In judicial or notarial proceedings, an expert report lacking rigorous methodological foundation is easily impeached by the opposing party, compromising the process or causing patrimonial indefensiveness in the client. In litigation, procedural deadlines leave no room for a second attempt: the report must withstand impeachment from the first filing.",
    "n4.cases.title": "Documented Cases",
    "n4.case.1": "Diego Velázquez Case (1984): detection at airport customs of a work attributed to the master, restored to the National Museum of Fine Arts following a joint technical opinion with Dr. Marta Arjona, President of the National Council of Cultural Heritage.",
    "n4.case.2": "Demétre Chiparus Sculpture Case (\"La gallinita ciega\"): interception and expert examination of the Art Déco bronze, marble, and ivory sculpture, which was being removed from the country without documentation.",
    "n4.case.3": "Official representation of Cuba at the UNESCO/OEI Cusco Forum (2020) on legal cooperation against illicit trafficking of cultural property.",
    "n4.services.title": "Specific Appraisal Services",
    "n4.service.1": "Judicial appraisal reports.",
    "n4.service.2": "Technical expert examination reports with documented chain of custody.",
    "n4.service.3": "Formal ratification of appraisal findings before the competent authority.",
    "n4.cta.main": "Request Expert Technical Assistance",
    "n4.cta.whatsapp": "Hello, I represent a law firm/notary office and require expert technical assistance for an art or heritage asset appraisal case.",
    "n4.cta.form": "Submit a Judicial Engagement Brief",

    // === NICHO 5: Insurers (aseguradoras-family-offices.html) ===
    "n5.hero.h1": "Fine Art Valuation for Insurers & Family Offices",
    "n5.hero.subtitle": "Insurable value opinions, collection audits, and claims appraisal for the international high-net-worth market.",
    "n5.value.text": "The appraisal methodology of Luis Manuel Almeida Luis carries international standing, grounded in the school of Dr. Alex J. Rosenberg, former president of the Appraisers Association of America. This methodological foundation has been applied in inventory, documentation, and appraisal campaigns of state-owned assets at embassies in more than 15 countries across Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and South America (1999 and 2018).",
    "n5.problem.text": "Insurance policies subscribed on outdated valuations or empirical estimates result in ruinous underinsurance or endless litigation between insurer and insured in case of total loss or partial damage. The cost of a deficient valuation is not paid when the policy is written, but on the day a claim reveals the gap between what was insured and what it actually costs to replace the piece.",
    "n5.cases.title": "Documented Cases",
    "n5.case.1": "Inventory, documentation, cataloguing, and appraisal campaign of Cuban cultural property at embassies in Spain, Italy, the Holy See, France, UNESCO-Paris, Portugal, Austria, Slovakia, Romania, Serbia, Algeria, Egypt, Lebanon, Qatar, Kuwait, Iran, and Bolivia (1999 and 2018).",
    "n5.case.2": "Symposium on Teaching Methodology in Art Appraisal, taught by Dr. Alex J. Rosenberg (New York University, 1999), followed by co-authorship of his reference book Tasación de Obras de Arte (2010).",
    "n5.services.title": "Specific Appraisal Services",
    "n5.service.1": "Corporate and family collection audits.",
    "n5.service.2": "Determination of replacement value for Fine Art Insurance policies.",
    "n5.service.3": "Claims damage appraisal.",
